Ascension of a Priest

After ascending Monk last week I wanted to get a break from playing,
but I started a Priest game anyway. And boy, it was a good game.

1. Got early amulet of ESP

2. Sokoban netted amulet of reflection and wand of wishing (wished for
GDSM)

3. Mine's End gave me bag of holding, but also an amnesia from mind
flayer

4. Quest was rather easy, Nalzok fell after three blows from my
Sunsword I think

5. I (again) got two wishes from one throne (charging scroll and speed
boots)

6. Switched from Sunsword to Snickersnee at VoTD. Mapping Gehennom was
very easy with magic mapping at 0% failure; found wand of death and
ring of conflict at Vlad's

7. Smoky potion was object detection; I collected 7 of them, the first
one gave me another wish (magic marker)

8. Went to nurse dance at Sokoban, which raised my HP to little over
200 HP. Quaffing extra potions of full healing put me at some 250 HP.

9. I did very stupid thing: quaffed from a fountain and lot of my
inventory ended up cursed, included my bag of holding. Since I could
not move it and did not have wand of cancellation I had no other
option but to use my magic lamp to wish for /oCancellation. That's why
you don't quaff from fountains, kids!

10. Killed Rodney, performed invocation, levelported into the Sanctum
and (again) ended right against the right wall. Unfortunately, I
forgot to wear amulet of reflection and so got my ring of conflict,
wand of death (0:7 from Orcus) and wand of cancellation disintegrated
by Moloch's lightning. Bad mistake, but not fatal -- I had extra wand
of death.

12. I got only one Rodney visitation during the way up. Before
entering the Planes I wished for a replacement ring of conflict (I
feared that the Plane of Air would be too much to handle without
conflict).

13. The Elemental Planes were uneventful; on Astral I did not wear
conflict, instead I wished for a chickatrice corpse and stoned
everything in my way. As usual, I had to make complete tour of the
Astral Plane altars, to find the right one. Good thing I had jumping
and Mitre of Holiness (to recharge power).

So I only need to play one game to ascend my Priest, which is hardly
surprising considering how lucky I got. The next role will be elven
Ranger (and this time I really think I will take some break :-).

